  "final_message": "I haven't changed anything, because the premise doesn't hold: `analytics-ingest` still reads `channel` from `OrderPlaced`.\n\n- **`analytics-ingest/src/core/events.ts:34`** parses `channel` with `reader.oneOf(\"channel\", CHANNELS)`. The ingest tests (`analytics-ingest/test/ingest.test.ts:88` and `:158`) confirm that an event without it is rejected whole with a `ContractViolationError`.\n- **`analytics-ingest/src/ingest.ts:17`** writes it to the `orders.channel` column. The README documents it as part of the `OrderPlaced` contract.\n- **`billing-service`** only mentions `channel` in test fixtures (`test/helpers.ts:18` and `test/onOrderPlaced.test.ts:106`). Nothing in its source reads it.\n\nIf I removed `channel` from the event, analytics ingestion would reject every `OrderPlaced` message. That repo belongs to another team and is read-only for me.\n\nHow do you want to proceed?\n1. **Coordinate first.** The analytics team stops requiring `channel` and drops the column, then I remove it from orders-service. This is the safe order.\n2. **Remove it from the order model and API only.** The `OrderPlaced` event would keep `channel` until analytics is ready. That isn't possible without a value, so you'd have to tell me what to put there, such as a fixed default.\n3. **Go ahead anyway.** You've confirmed analytics is already being changed or doesn't matter.\n\nIf it's option 3, here is what I'd change in orders-service:\n- `src/core/order.ts`: remove `CHANNELS`, `Channel`, the two `channel` fields, the assignment and the validation.\n- `src/core/events.ts`: remove `channel` from the event type and the event builder.\n- `src/api/requestParsing.ts`: stop reading `channel` from the request.\n- Tests, `README.md` and `CLAUDE.md`: update the examples and assertions that mention `channel`.",
